According to Law N° 68/24 of 30/05/24 and Law N° 71/24 of 28/05/24, a person aged 18 or older may be adopted if they meet the following criteria:
1º having neither hearing impairment nor multiple disabilities;
2º being at least 21 years old;
3º being able to give his or her informed consent.
However, a person who meets these requirements but has a hearing impairment or multiple disabilities may be adopted under special conditions.

The adoption record shows that you meet the age requirement. The other stated condition is that you must have heard before you can give informed consent. The provided text does not specify

According to Law N° 68/24 of 30/05/24 and Law N° 69/24 of 17/05/24, offences are classified as follows:

1º an offence of the first degree if it is punishable by life imprisonment or by imprisonment for a term of more than 5 years but less than 10 years;
2º an offence of the second degree if it is punishable by imprisonment for a term of at least 10 years and not more than 15 years;
3º an offence of the third degree if it is punishable by imprisonment for a term of at least 15 years and not more than 20 years.

